  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.2. Increased capacity of the member States to apply international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">CEACR Observation on C 111:

&quot; The Committee notes with satisfaction that section 248 of the Labour Code of 2003, as revised in 2020, limits the prohibition on working in underground works to pregnant women, women who have recently given birth and women who breastfeed, as well as in activities that present risks to their safety or health or which may have an impact on their pregnancy or lactation.&#x201D;

 At the request of the constituents in Moldova, the Office organized a tripartite workshop in Chisinau, Moldova on &quot;Mainstreaming gender into Labour law&#x201D; from 10 to 11 December 2015 which resulted in the above amendment of the Labour Code in 2020. The workshop took place following a cooperation between the ILO and UNIFEM within UNIFEM&#x2019;s &quot;Women&#x2019;s Economic Empowerment&#x201D; Programme.
This was a follow-up activity to the tripartite workshop that was held in 2010 on &quot;Reviewing the labour code through the gender lens&#x201D; in cooperation with UNIFEM in Chisinau.</narrative>
   </description>
