  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.1. Increased capacity of the member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ratification of the ILO Occupational Health Services Convention, 1985 (No. 161) became part of the Government Action Plan 2020-2023 and was included in the Decent Work Country Programme of Moldova (2021-2024). 
On March 4th 2021, the Moldovan Parliament passed legislation ratifying the ILO Occupational Health Services Convention, 1985 (No. 161). By taking this action, Moldova pledged to strengthen the governance of its Occupational Safety and Health (OSH) system, to give higher priority to diagnosing occupational diseases, and to create systems that lead employers to report promptly and fully on work-related injuries and diseases. The ILO supported the conduct of a feasibility study for Moldova&#x2019;s ratification of the ILO Occupational Health Services Convention, 1985 (No. 161) by a national consultant. Based on this report and ILO&apos;s technical comments, the ILO organized a Tripartite Workshop on the ratification on 31 May 2013.</narrative>
   </description>
